FreeWheel, a Comcast company, provides comprehensive ad platforms for publishers, advertisers, and media buyers. Powered by premium video content, robust data, and advanced technology, we’re making it easier for buyers and sellers to transact across all screens, data types, and sales channels. As a global company, we have offices in nine countries and can insert advertisements around the world.

Job Summary

FreeWheel is looking for an analyst to join our Global Reporting and Analytics team. The Global Reporting and Analytics team acts as strategic partners across the organization by helping stakeholders make fast-paced, data-driven decisions. This role is a vital component for FreeWheel's Marketplace business, which enables the most premium video inventory owners and buyers - such as TV Programmers, MVPDs, major digital media publishers, advertisers, agencies, and DSPs - to drive successful business outcomes at scale. In this role, you will work cross-functionally with internal teams to uncover growth opportunities, identify product enhancements, and develop robust reporting solutions. The successful candidate will require excellent communication and problem-solving skills, and the ability to think strategically while being analytical and detail oriented. The Analyst II will report directly to: Senior Manager, Global Reporting and Analytics. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work for Comcast in the United States without a current or potential future need for sponsorship.

Job Description

Core Responsibilities

Develop and maintain reporting of Digital TV key business metrics using different BI tools for Freewheel constituents, including internal users, external clients, and executives.
Conduct regular analysis of large-scale data sets to uncover opportunities to improve overall sales, inventory management, and yield strategies.
Prototype and develop automated reporting solutions to monitor the health of the business.
Collaborate with business stakeholders and technology leaders to build out new product features and business processes.
 Ensure data quality and cleanliness for consistent and accurate reporting.
Creating ETL processes to accommodate changes in source systems and new business user requirements.
Implement AI-powered advanced analytics capabilities that enabled end users to generate insights, identify trends, and make faster, data-driven decisions.

Qualifications

Bachelor's degree in quantitative field preferred.
1+ years of experience using data and analysis to drive business outcomes.
Strong knowledge of SQL.
Experience with a scripting language (Python or R).
Experience with Visualization BI tools (Looker and Tableau).
Advanced Excel Skills.
Experience in advertising technology is a plus.
Skilled in synthesizing detailed analysis into clear narratives, facilitating strategic discussions across technical and business stakeholders.

Demonstrated experience with the required technical skills must be evident on the resume, including hands-on use of SQL, Python or R, BI visualization tools (Looker and/or Tableau), advanced Excel, and data analysis to drive business outcomes. Candidates should clearly showcase these skills through relevant professional experience and accomplishments.

